cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DIRE: Disease Incidence and Resource Estimator"
message: >-
  If you use this software or its data pipelines, please cite both
  this software and the underlying methodology paper.
type: software
authors:
  - name: New Light Technologies, Inc.
    website: "https://newlighttechnologies.com"
  - name: University of California, San Diego
    website: "https://gps.ucsd.edu"
repository-code: "https://github.com/DIRE-OSI/platform"
url: "https://dire.impact.nltglobal.com"
abstract: >-
  DIRE (Disease Incidence and Resource Estimator) is an open-science machine-learning
  platform producing 1-, 2-, and 3-month-ahead disease-incidence forecasts at
  sub-national administrative granularity. Initial coverage is dengue and malaria
  in Peru and Brazil, with additional countries and diseases being onboarded. It
  integrates remote-sensing and climate covariates with epidemiological surveillance
  data in an ensemble model (CatBoost, SVM, LSTM synthesized with a Random Forest).
keywords:
  - dengue
  - malaria
  - epidemiology
  - forecasting
  - machine-learning
  - remote-sensing
  - public-health
  - open-science
  - Peru
  - Brazil
license: Apache-2.0
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      A machine learning approach to dengue and malaria incidence forecasting
    authors:
      - family-names: Sebastianelli
        given-names: A.
    year: 2024
    journal: Scientific Reports
    doi: 10.1038/s41598-024-52796-9
